From a2cdfeec03004c7f812f91d69ab48cc8ff03e6c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:16:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Remove synthetic climate/CO2 fallbacks, cache archive trends

- climate.py: drop the random-noise monthly fallback; archive failures now
  return no months plus a reason. Missing monthly values are null, not 0.0.
  Successful six-month archive results are cached for 6 h (day-keyed).
- mock_data.py: CO2 returns null (with co2_data_source) instead of a
  hardcoded 424.0 when NOAA has never been reachable.
- main.py: /environment no longer crashes on empty trends; reports
  rainfall and CO2 provenance.
- ui.js (v47): rainfall card shows n/a with the reason; CO2 badged LIVE
  only for real readings.
- benchmark_latency.py: reports first vs warm requests separately; no
  fallback timing; server output no longer piped.
- New tests/test_climate_trends.py (16 tests); docs updated (117 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Shu2juUq1xdP9kBJeGEf1b
